WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.030
Hi, welcome back to Nagarjuna

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.250
and the emptiness of the Medicine Buddha.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.970
And we've reached the next
chapter which is Chapter 12.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.570
Don't forget our goal
is to finish 27 chapters

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.180
in five years.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:19.040
And this is the third year and
we're making good progress.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.610
We're already to the twelfth chapter.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:25.730
And again this is a parīkṣā
(pariksha) which means what?

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.310
An investigation.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.900
And this time we're going to
investigate duḥkha (duhkha).

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:32.733
- [Woman] Suffering.

00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:33.570
- Suffering, yay!

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.270
So I don't know about you,

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:37.890
but you feel like, oh finally

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.710
he got to this subject.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:44.550
I would like to investigate
all the messing in my life,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.691
all the messes in my life.

00:00:46.691 --> 00:00:51.015
I would like to investigate and
find out why they're happening.

00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:54.410
So like why did this COVID come

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.500
and why is my partner grumpy sometimes?

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.360
Why does my dog pee in the house?

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.870
And big things like that, you know.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.596
So this is called

00:01:06.596 --> 00:01:10.300
BDAG GIS BYAS PA DANG
GZHAN GYIS BYAS PA BRTAG PA

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:15.300
which means an examination
of investigation

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.250
of is the pain, the trouble in my life,

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.130
is it coming from me?

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:24.610
Or is it coming from something else?

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.693
And the "me" here is BDAG.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:33.830
So that can also mean,
does the trouble in my life

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.740
come from the trouble in my life,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.340
or does it come from something else?

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.440
Does the trouble in my life come

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.720
from itself or from something else?

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.110
I'll say it again.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.370
Do the problems in my life come

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.480
from the problems in my life,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.170
or do they come from something else?

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:58.170
Then, actually, Nagarjuna
splits it into two.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.090
Do the problems in my life

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.440
come from the problems in my life,

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:04.820
or do they come from something else?

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.100
And who gives me the problems in my life?

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.480
Is it me or is it somebody else?

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.720
Who gives me trouble?

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.050
Is it always me giving myself trouble?

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:19.610
So we're discussing self and other

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.800
in two different contexts.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.120
Does the pain cause itself,

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.440
or does something else cause the pain?

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.110
Do I cause myself pain?

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.870
Do I pain myself,

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.060
or does someone else pain me?

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.880
So those are the questions

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.630
that we're going to explore in chapter 12.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.763
Let's go to the first verse.

00:02:41.409 --> 00:02:43.184
,KHA CIG SDUG BSNGAL BDAG GIS BYAS,

00:02:43.184 --> 00:02:45.150
,GZHAN GYIS BYAS DANG GNYI GAS BYAS,

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.825
,RGYU MED PA LAS 'BYUNG BAR 'DOD,

00:02:47.825 --> 00:02:51.008
,DE NI BYA BAR MI RUNG NGO,

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.000
Then Nagarjuna gives you four options

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.370
about: does pain cause itself?

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.070
Forget me or you.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.530
That's not what we're talking
about in the first part.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.920
We're talking about,

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.800
does the trouble in my life
cause the trouble in my life,

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.770
or does something else than the trouble

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.500
in my life cause the trouble in my life?

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.820
And Nagarjuna starts out
and he says, you know,

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.730
this question is discussed

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.500
by four different groups of people.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.070
There's four philosophical schools

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.940
in ancient India, 2,000 years ago,

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.390
who have an opinion on this question.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:35.090
KHA CIG means different
people say different things.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.450
What?

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.385
First choice. Some of them say

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:43.518
SDUG BSNGAL BDAG GIS BYAS

00:03:43.518 --> 00:03:47.530
The trouble in my life comes
from the trouble in my life.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.760
That's the first opinion.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.950
All right? From itself.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.779
Now, second opinion.

00:03:53.779 --> 00:03:55.010
GZHAN GYIS BYAS

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.590
What's that?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.280
Yeah, because somebody else...

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.423
Something other than
the trouble in my life

00:04:00.423 --> 00:04:01.720
causes the trouble in my life.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.640
That's the second opinion.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:04.893
Third opinion.

00:04:04.893 --> 00:04:07.250
GNYI GAS BYAS

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.030
It's both of you guys.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.830
The suffering, the trouble in your life

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.180
causes the trouble in your life,

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.770
and there's things that aren't
the trouble in your life

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.052
that also bring trouble in your life.

00:04:15.052 --> 00:04:17.070
Exactly the same thing.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.949
Third choice.

00:04:18.949 --> 00:04:21.800
Oh! RGYU MED

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.510
Yeah, neither one.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.862
Nothing causes the trouble in
your life. It just happens.

00:04:27.862 --> 00:04:31.162
LAS 'BYUNG BAR 'DOD
DE NI BYA BAR MI RUNG NGO

00:04:31.162 --> 00:04:32.890
Hey, you're all wrong.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:35.220
Wait a minute. One of
them has to be right.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.260
There's only four possibilities.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:39.130
He says no.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.710
And I think this is a good
place to learn some Sanskrit.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:46.740
So in different parts of these classes

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.940
we've been learning
different kinds of Sanskrit.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.980
And there's some Sanskrit right here

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.420
which I thought it would be useful

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.280
to throw it in right away.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:05:01.280
And that is: by itself; by something else;

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.290
by both; by neither.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:08.150
Let's learn the Sanskrit for
those four possibilities.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:12.480
Then let's learn the Sanskrit
for trouble in your life

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.531
because that's how we spend our life.

00:05:15.531 --> 00:05:17.538
So here's the Sanskrit.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:23.550
The first one, svayaṃ kṛta (svayam kirta),

00:05:23.637 --> 00:05:25.187
svayam kirta.

00:05:25.187 --> 00:05:28.373
Svayam means came from itself.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.025
Kirta means made.

00:05:31.025 --> 00:05:35.550
The trouble in your life svayam
kirta, "comes from itself."

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.920
The trouble in your
life comes from itself.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.087
In Tibetan, BDAG GIS BYAS
-- it comes from itself.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:47.480
This "svaya" in Sanskrit has
pieces like "su" and "aya".

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.710
And su means yourself.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:53.357
And aya makes it a noun, selfness.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:59.250
And we see this su in English
when we say "suicide".

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.970
"Cide" means to kill.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.600
And "sui" means yourself.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:08.240
Self comes from sui, su,

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.250
and solitary comes from su.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:14.980
So all of those words
come from this svaya.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.840
Also the Indo-European is s(w)e.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.050
And that came into "self" and "secret".

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:23.485
So all of these words meaning self.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.111
Kirta.

00:06:26.111 --> 00:06:26.944
[coughing]

00:06:26.944 --> 00:06:30.320
Kirta comes from a verb √kṛ
(kir) which means "to do".

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:35.320
That's the root of the word karma.

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:38.940
And kir just in general
means "to do" something.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:43.770
English cognates are
cereal, create, and karma.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.310
Cereal. There's a time in history

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:49.720
when C changed to S sound.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:54.053
And originally it was ka, so
"create" and then "cereal".

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:58.080
All right, so these all mean "to make".

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:01.360
Now, the second option is that things are

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:04.184
parakṛta (parakirta).

00:07:04.184 --> 00:07:07.390
The trouble in my life
comes from something

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:09.900
other than the trouble in my life,

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.090
or the trouble in my life is caused

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:14.290
by someone else other than me.

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:15.340
Second choice.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:18.720
"Para" just means
somebody else, other guys.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:21.419
All right, third choice.

00:07:21.419 --> 00:07:25.419
Dvābhyāṃ kṛta (dvabhyan kirta),
dvabhyan kirta.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:30.066
The trouble in my life comes from both,

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:35.616
me and other people or by itself
and from other things, both.

00:07:36.607 --> 00:07:38.740
Dva means two.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:43.120
That's why the number two has a W in it.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:48.120
It's also, the W is the B
in "bicycle", for example.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.203
And the word "divide".

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:56.175
Or this fourth choice
is "ahetuka", ahetuka.

00:07:57.193 --> 00:07:58.132
Hetu means?

00:07:58.132 --> 00:08:00.244
- [Woman] Cause.
- Cause. A?

00:08:00.244 --> 00:08:01.807
- [Woman] Not.
- Not, okay.

00:08:01.807 --> 00:08:04.400
"Ka" means made by.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:08.650
Yeah, not made by causes, ahetuka.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:11.160
So the last possibility is that

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.500
the trouble in your life
just comes to you at random.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:17.550
It's not brought about by
you or by other people.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:18.770
It doesn't come from itself.

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:21.090
It doesn't come from something else.

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:22.500
I like this word, duḥkham (duhkham).

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.757
I mean, I don't like
duhkham, but I like the word.

00:08:25.757 --> 00:08:26.784
Duhkha.

00:08:26.784 --> 00:08:30.309
Duh stands for D-U-S.

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:34.290
The S changes to H in this context.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.860
And so "dus" means bad.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:38.190
I don't know, did you call people

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:40.697
[expletive] in your high school?

00:08:40.697 --> 00:08:42.570
[chuckling]

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.893
I'm sorry. Forget that.

00:08:46.085 --> 00:08:49.860
Dus means bad.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:53.150
It came into English as D-Y-S.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:57.940
I think through the Greek,
"dysfunctional" or "disease".

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:04.260
And then the "kha" means
the open hub of a wheel.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:08.230
Traditionally duhkha is explained

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.320
as meaning "a squeaky wheel".

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.514
You know, they say what?

00:09:13.514 --> 00:09:15.848
The squeaky wheel makes the most noise.

00:09:15.848 --> 00:09:17.130
- [Woman] The squeaky
wheel gets the grease.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.780
- Oh yeah.

00:09:19.893 --> 00:09:22.440
Anyway, troublesome people
make the most noise,

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.960
something like that.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.630
So duhkha is traditionally explained

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:31.370
as being a bad connection
on your wheel on your cart.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:35.118
And then it goes...
[mimicking squeaking]

00:09:35.118 --> 00:09:39.640
Kha is also found in
Indo-European as √ghāi, ghai.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.743
That means...
[mimicking yawning]

00:09:41.743 --> 00:09:42.780
Ghai.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:46.815
It means to yawn or to
gape with your mouth.

00:09:46.815 --> 00:09:51.318
So duhkha basically is just a big mouth.

00:09:51.318 --> 00:09:52.370
A big, bad mouth.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:53.920
And it means trouble.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.336
Where does the duhkha,

00:09:55.336 --> 00:09:58.640
where does the trouble might've come from?

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:01.913
Is it svayan kirta?

00:10:01.913 --> 00:10:04.720
Svayan kirta, does it
come from me somehow?

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.529
Parakirta, does it come
from somebody else somehow?

00:10:08.529 --> 00:10:12.880
Dvabhyan kirta, is it coming
from me and other people?

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.140
Or is it ahetuka?

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:16.440
Or does it just happen?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:18.270
Things happen.

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:19.720
All right that's the chapter

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.480
that we're going to be looking at.

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.730
Let's go to the next verse.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.272
,GAL TE BDAG GIS BYAS GYUR NA,

00:10:33.272 --> 00:10:34.829
,DE PHYIR BRTEN NAS 'BYUNG MI 'GYUR,

00:10:34.829 --> 00:10:36.637
,GANG PHYIR PHUNG PO 'DI DAG LA,

00:10:36.637 --> 00:10:38.896
,BRTEN NAS PHUNG PO DE DAG 'BYUNG,

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.180
When we're discussing the possibility

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:47.331
that pain has come from pain itself,

00:10:48.303 --> 00:10:51.120
Nagarjuna says, what I mean is,

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:57.290
did the mortal falling
apart body that you have

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.770
and mind that you have now,

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:02.670
did that come from a
mortal falling apart body

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:04.647
and mind in the past life?

00:11:04.647 --> 00:11:06.820
That's what it means when he says

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:10.060
that suffering causes suffering itself.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:13.513
Is it the nature of your
body and mind to suffer?

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.750
And let's look at the possibility

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:21.600
that your body and mind
which are falling apart,

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:23.985
and you can't stop it normally.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:29.460
And it's funny the things that
people do to try to stop it.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:31.419
I think half the things we try to do

00:11:31.419 --> 00:11:34.270
to stop the suffering, the falling
apart of our body and mind,

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:37.760
they just accelerate the falling
apart of our body and mind.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.578
Anyway.

00:11:39.578 --> 00:11:42.370
GAL TE, he says here,

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:47.370
So Nagarjuna says, "When I talk
about pain coming from pain

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.690
"what I'm really talking about

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:53.360
"is what caused your
body and mind right now

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.260
"that's falling apart."

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:58.170
And let's look at the first possibility

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:01.110
that it's coming from the
same thing in the past.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:03.870
You had a body and mind
that was falling apart.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:06.698
And then it created a body
and mind that's falling apart.

00:12:06.698 --> 00:12:08.094
So here we go.

00:12:08.094 --> 00:12:10.654
GAL TE BDAG GIS BYAS GYUR NA

00:12:10.654 --> 00:12:13.530
If the problems you have in your life

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:16.078
are coming from the problems in your life,

00:12:16.078 --> 00:12:18.057
DE PHYIR BRTEN NAS 'BYUNG MI 'GYUR

00:12:18.057 --> 00:12:22.380
then we can say that it did not come about

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.670
by depending on something else.

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:27.740
If the trouble in your
life has been caused

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.720
by the trouble in your life,

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.270
then we can say there's
no dependence there.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.840
It's not like the trouble in your life

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.327
has to depend on trouble in your life

00:12:36.327 --> 00:12:39.168
because it's already trouble in your life.

00:12:39.168 --> 00:12:41.234
GANG PHYIR PHUNG PO 'DI DAG LA

00:12:41.234 --> 00:12:43.770
BRTEN NAS PHUNG PO DE DAG 'BYUNG

00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:48.770
Actually, I should say that
even when you say suffering...

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:52.320
Now, Nagarjuna is correcting the guy.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:54.650
I would say though that if you have

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:57.160
a body and mind that's falling apart,

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:59.250
it's a sign that you had a body and mind

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.600
that was falling apart before.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.020
So maybe last life you had

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.910
a body and mind that was falling apart.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.676
You did things.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:11.334
You did not so nice things

00:13:11.334 --> 00:13:12.940
because your body and
mind was falling apart.

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:14.780
And then now in this life your body

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:16.140
and mind is falling apart.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.900
So falling apart causes falling apart.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.166
That's okay.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.538
And then by the way, he says,

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:31.940
"In that case, if pain causes pain,

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:36.940
then could you have come from your death?"

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.810
And he says no.

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:42.920
It's not correct to say
that the falling apart

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.090
body and mind of your last life

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.260
caused the falling apart
body and mind of this life

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:52.650
because the body and mind falling
apart in this life started,

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.080
and that one was ending.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.950
So if they're the same thing,

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.780
they wouldn't have a cause and effect.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.950
It could not have come from my death.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:02.570
I cannot come from my death.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:03.533
Picture.

00:14:07.494 --> 00:14:09.710
GANG GI PHYIR NA 'CHI DUS
KYI SDUG BSNGAL GYI PHUNG PO

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:11.360
'DI DAG LA BRTEN NAS SKYE
BA'I CHAR GTOGS KYI PHUNG PO

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.993
DE DAG 'BYUNG BA'I PHYIR,

00:14:16.594 --> 00:14:18.443
SDUG BSNGAL DE CHOS CAN

00:14:18.443 --> 00:14:21.026
SDUG BSNGAL RANG YOD NA RANG
GIS BSKYED MI DGOS SHING

00:14:21.026 --> 00:14:23.134
MED NA RANG GIS BSKYED MI NUS PA'I PHYIR,

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.240
If your suffering body

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:32.010
and mind came from your
past suffering body

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.420
and mind, then since
your past body and mind

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:36.480
where already suffering, they didn't have

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:39.540
to create more suffering because
they were already suffering.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.130
Nobody made them suffering.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:44.829
The cause was suffering.

00:14:44.829 --> 00:14:46.290
So the result was suffering.

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:50.370
So no new suffering was made.

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.204
No new suffering was made.

00:14:52.204 --> 00:14:55.150
SDUG BSNGAL RANG YOD NA
RANG GIS BSKYED MI DGOS

00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:58.090
If your nature is to suffer,

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:01.103
then no one has to make you suffer.

00:15:01.103 --> 00:15:03.920
SHING MED NA RANG GIS BSKYED MI NUS

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:06.530
If your nature is to suffer,

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:09.100
then you don't have to do anything.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:10.820
You're going to suffer anyway.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.520
If your nature is not to suffer,

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.650
and you try to make yourself suffer,

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:18.375
you couldn't do it anyway.

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:23.420
If your nature is not to suffer,

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:25.140
then nothing could make you suffer.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:27.573
If your nature is to suffer,

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.670
then nobody would have to make you suffer

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:33.420
because you're already suffering.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:37.980
Next verse.

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:44.752
,GAL TE 'DI LAS DE GZHAN ZHING,

00:15:44.752 --> 00:15:47.801
,GAL TE DE LAS 'DI GZHAN NA,

00:15:47.801 --> 00:15:49.801
,SDUG BSNGAL GZHAN GYIS BYAS 'GYUR ZHING,

00:15:49.801 --> 00:15:54.775
,GZHAN DE DAG GIS DE BYAS 'GYUR,

00:15:56.112 --> 00:15:59.413
This is how Choney Lama reads this one.

00:15:59.413 --> 00:16:03.058
GAL TE 'DI LAS DE GZHAN ZHING

00:16:03.058 --> 00:16:06.920
If the body and mind falling apart

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:10.365
that you took in this life was coming from

00:16:10.365 --> 00:16:14.872
body and mind at your last death,

00:16:14.872 --> 00:16:16.240
which is GZHAN.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:21.240
GZHAN means is the falling
apart body and mind of this life

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:26.700
is it your body and mind
falling apart in your last life?

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:27.650
Yes or no?

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:31.290
Is your body and mind
falling apart in this life

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.840
your body and mind falling
apart in your last life?

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.318
- Are they the same thing?

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.960
- No, they are the same experience,

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:43.960
but one happens first and
then the other one happens.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.983
So can we say that falling apart

00:16:45.983 --> 00:16:49.270
of your body and mind in this life

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.200
is different from the falling apart

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.860
of your body and mind in your past life?

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.619
- Is it different things?

00:16:56.619 --> 00:16:58.145
- Yeah, they're different things.

00:16:58.145 --> 00:17:00.760
GAL TE DE LAS 'DI GZHAN NA

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:03.718
If they were really different things,

00:17:03.718 --> 00:17:06.001
,SDUG BSNGAL GZHAN GYIS BYAS 'GYUR ZHING,

00:17:06.001 --> 00:17:08.920
,GZHAN DE DAG GIS DE BYAS 'GYUR,

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:11.477
then you could say...

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:17.580
If they were different,
maybe you could say

00:17:18.606 --> 00:17:20.470
that the falling apart
of your body and mind

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:24.350
in your last life has
caused the falling apart

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:26.510
of your body and mind in this life.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.000
That's okay.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:31.660
If you had a body and mind
falling apart in your last life

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:34.060
so you did mean things to other people

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:36.720
to try to fix your falling
apart body and mind,

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.170
then you get a new falling
apart body and mind.

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:41.790
Are those the same body and mind,

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.624
or are they different body and mind?

00:17:44.624 --> 00:17:46.210
- So they're different, right?

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:47.580
- They have to be.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:49.560
- Then they never touch.

00:17:54.696 --> 00:17:56.110
They never make contact.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:59.210
So how can two things
that never make contact

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:00.928
affect each other?

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.510
If you play or shoot a billiard ball

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:07.340
and it hits another billiard ball,

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:09.117
there has to be a point of contact.

00:18:09.117 --> 00:18:11.440
And the motion of the first ball

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.560
creates the motion of the second ball.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.680
If your past life's
suffering body and mind

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:21.290
impelled your present life's
suffering body and mind,

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:23.580
then they should've made
contact at some point.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.300
But if things exist the
way you think they do,

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:29.443
outside of your seeds, they
can never make contact.

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:31.443
They cannot make contact.

00:18:31.443 --> 00:18:32.960
We already went through that.

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.350
It's like your foot on the...

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:36.160
Where's the middle part of your foot?

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:38.540
Where does the past meet the present?

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:41.130
Where does the past meet the future?

00:18:41.130 --> 00:18:45.550
There cannot be contact between two things

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:49.970
if they are self-existently separate.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:53.290
If they exist by themselves
from their own side,

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:55.601
they cannot make contact

00:18:55.601 --> 00:18:59.080
because they would have
to overlap and they can't.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:01.700
If they did overlap, then your past life

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:06.340
would be your present
life for a little time.

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:07.660
They can't touch.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.600
There's nowhere where they can touch.

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:13.650
There's no place where they can touch.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.560
If your past life touches
your present life,

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:18.340
then the place where they touch would be

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.400
both your present life and your past life.

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:21.680
And that's not possible.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.160
They have to be separate.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:25.460
If they're completely separate like that,

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:28.877
then by the time your past
life messed up body and mind...

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:35.680
Sorry, if it's still there
you haven't died yet,

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:38.452
and you can't have a
future body and mind yet.

00:19:38.452 --> 00:19:40.280
If you have a future body and mind,

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.810
then your past body and mind already died.

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:45.330
A thing which is already gone cannot have

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:47.500
a relationship with something that's here.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:49.460
Not possible.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:52.900
Something that came the moment before

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:56.310
can never cause something
which is here now

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:59.650
because there's no time for them to touch.

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:02.550
Either the past thing would have to be,

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.880
have its toe in the present,

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:07.688
or the present thing would
have to have the edge

00:20:07.688 --> 00:20:09.320
of its bottom in the past.

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:13.410
Somebody would have to cross
the line for them to touch.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:14.710
Got it?

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:15.543
And it's not possible.

00:20:15.543 --> 00:20:16.530
It's not possible.

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:18.610
Don't blame something else

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.670
for causing your current suffering.

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:22.960
It can't be.

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:26.110
If it's gone, it can't do anything.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:30.025
If it's not gone, you're
still in your past life.

00:20:30.025 --> 00:20:30.858
Okay.

00:20:30.858 --> 00:20:32.790
All right, whew.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:33.623
All right.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:39.523
I have a picture here of
a finger and a cactus.

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:46.180
This is different from the
other finger and cactus picture.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:47.490
- Why, Geshe-la?

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:50.873
- There's a space between
the finger and the cactus.

00:20:52.077 --> 00:20:57.077
If things never touch each
other, you can't get hurt.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:03.110
If your finger never touches
the cactus, you can't get hurt.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:05.430
And the fact is that you can't,

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:09.470
your finger, your present suffering

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:12.510
cannot touch your past life's
suffering, not possible.

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:14.115
Cannot.

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:20.050
Rebecca, if they never touch,
can one hurt the other?

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:22.900
No, if they never touch, then
one cannot cause the other.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:26.910
Now, if you like insist, yeah,

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:29.110
my current life suffering happens.

00:21:29.110 --> 00:21:31.133
Forget, I don't care about it.

00:21:31.133 --> 00:21:32.670
And my past life's suffering caused it.

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:34.910
- Did they touch? - No.

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:37.160
- Can a cactus hurt your
finger without touching

00:21:37.160 --> 00:21:39.770
if your present life
can have trouble caused

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:42.270
by your past life without touching?

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:44.360
- Yeah, they can.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:48.800
- Okay, so you should run around
like this all day, ow, ow, ow.

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:52.877
- Why? - Because there's
cactus near Phoenix.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:56.440
And it doesn't have to
touch you to hurt you.

00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:58.592
- Okay, Geshe-la, it does
have to touch me to hurt you.

00:21:58.592 --> 00:22:01.350
- Okay, then your past life
has to touch your present life.

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:02.900
- Yeah, well, what's wrong with that?

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.120
- They have to overlap.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:07.230
Then part of your past life
has to be in the present

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:08.700
to touch your present life,

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:10.160
or part of your present life has

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:12.317
to be in the past to get
touched by your past life.

00:22:12.317 --> 00:22:14.470
But that's not possible
because your present life

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.590
is different from your past life.

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:18.720
If your present life had
to touch your past life,

00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:21.950
then you would be in your past life.

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:23.450
Got it?

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:26.200
It's not possible what
you think is happening.

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:28.830
It's not even possible
what the Buddha kept saying

00:22:28.830 --> 00:22:30.320
that what you did your past life

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:31.990
is causing you suffering in this life.

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:34.360
That's not possible.

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:38.380
The Buddha? Something's wrong.

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:41.490
A cactus that you never could touch

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:43.680
is making your finger hurt.

00:22:43.680 --> 00:22:45.700
That's the same thing.

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:48.000
I'll say it again. Don't look so confused.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.020
Or look confused, that's okay.

00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:52.887
If what you did in your
past life is causing

00:22:52.887 --> 00:22:55.173
you suffering in the present life,

00:22:55.173 --> 00:22:56.840
then the past life has
to touch the present life

00:22:56.840 --> 00:23:00.180
in the same way that your
finger has to touch a cactus.

00:23:00.180 --> 00:23:02.230
And if your finger can
hurt without touching

00:23:02.230 --> 00:23:04.920
the cactus, and if your
present life can have trouble

00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:06.970
without touching your past life,

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:10.420
then because there's cactuses in Arizona,

00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:12.310
every time you cross the state line

00:23:12.310 --> 00:23:13.920
your finger should start hurting.

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:15.020
- Why?

00:23:15.020 --> 00:23:18.560
- Because without touching,
they can hurt you.

00:23:18.560 --> 00:23:20.851
- What do you mean? What's
that got to do with it?

00:23:20.851 --> 00:23:23.030
Because without your past life touching

00:23:23.030 --> 00:23:25.260
your present life, the
events of your past life

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:29.337
can hurt your present life,
according to you, Buddha.

00:23:29.337 --> 00:23:30.170
Got it?

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:31.570
But they can't touch.

00:23:31.570 --> 00:23:34.420
If they touch, then the very beginning

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:37.510
of your present life would
have to be in your past life,

00:23:37.510 --> 00:23:39.250
or the very end of your past life

00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:41.380
would have to be in your present life.

00:23:41.380 --> 00:23:46.380
And then there wouldn't be a difference
between past life and present life.

00:23:46.593 --> 00:23:47.840
It doesn't make sense.

00:23:47.840 --> 00:23:50.180
- Geshe-la, why are we talking
about this stuff? Who cares?

00:23:50.180 --> 00:23:52.673
Who cares because you can't stop suffering

00:23:52.673 --> 00:23:54.630
unless you figure out
where it's coming from.

00:23:54.630 --> 00:23:57.865
And it's not coming from your past life

00:23:57.865 --> 00:24:00.660
because your past life can't
touch your present life.

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:02.616
- Well, where's it coming from?

00:24:02.616 --> 00:24:06.630
- You know, you'll get there. Okay.

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:08.321
All right, next verse.

00:24:09.483 --> 00:24:12.433
,GAL TE GANG ZAG BDAG GIS NI,

00:24:12.433 --> 00:24:14.690
,SDUG BSNGAL BYAS NA GANG BDAG GIS,

00:24:14.690 --> 00:24:16.748
,SDUG BSNGAL BYAS PA'I GANG ZAG NI,

00:24:16.748 --> 00:24:19.581
,SDUG BSNGAL MA GTOGS GANG ZHIG YIN,

00:24:20.660 --> 00:24:24.024
If some kind of... now it's a person.

00:24:24.024 --> 00:24:25.580
All right, let's say

00:24:25.580 --> 00:24:30.426
if someone else could hurt me, then

00:24:30.426 --> 00:24:32.167
,SDUG BSNGAL BYAS NA GANG BDAG GIS,

00:24:32.167 --> 00:24:34.382
,SDUG BSNGAL BYAS PA'I GANG ZAG NI,

00:24:34.382 --> 00:24:36.393
then that person who caused me pain

00:24:36.393 --> 00:24:39.289
SDUG BSNGAL MA GTOGS GANG ZHIG YIN

00:24:39.289 --> 00:24:40.830
must cause me pain all the time.

00:24:40.830 --> 00:24:42.900
Or they would be pain itself.

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:47.680
If another person can pain
me, then they are pain.

00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:57.520
If another person can pain
me, then they are pain.

00:24:57.520 --> 00:24:59.140
Got it?

00:24:59.140 --> 00:25:01.070
If another person can...

00:25:01.070 --> 00:25:03.480
We're always blaming our
problems on other people,

00:25:03.480 --> 00:25:06.330
all the time, every moment of the day.

00:25:06.330 --> 00:25:09.478
But if a person could make you feel pain,

00:25:09.478 --> 00:25:12.660
then they would have to be pain.

00:25:12.660 --> 00:25:16.394
Because you're feeling
pain when you touch them.

00:25:16.394 --> 00:25:17.477
Got it?

00:25:20.377 --> 00:25:21.970
And then you could go a different way.

00:25:21.970 --> 00:25:23.830
I think you could take
this a different way.

00:25:23.830 --> 00:25:25.938
And Choney Lama, if you read Choney Lama,

00:25:25.938 --> 00:25:27.013
you can take it this way.

00:25:27.013 --> 00:25:29.371
You can look at the picture here.

00:25:32.980 --> 00:25:37.690
I don't know, this is a guy in an office.

00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:41.623
I don't know if this ever
happened to you in a job

00:25:42.610 --> 00:25:44.540
that your boss is yelling at you.

00:25:44.540 --> 00:25:46.060
I don't know.

00:25:46.060 --> 00:25:48.930
It's almost the definition of a job.

00:25:50.580 --> 00:25:52.700
So the boss is yelling at the guy.

00:25:52.700 --> 00:25:55.030
Now, who's hurting whom?

00:25:55.030 --> 00:25:56.960
Wait, stay there, yeah good.

00:25:56.960 --> 00:25:59.200
- Who's hurting whom?

00:26:01.050 --> 00:26:02.940
- The boss is hurting the employee, right?

00:26:02.940 --> 00:26:04.590
The employee looks sad.

00:26:04.590 --> 00:26:06.660
The boss looks happy

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:08.701
because he gets to be the boss.

00:26:08.701 --> 00:26:09.940
And he's hurting the person.

00:26:09.940 --> 00:26:14.940
So you can say the boss
hurt the employee, right?

00:26:15.477 --> 00:26:18.227
Did the employee hurt themself?

00:26:20.350 --> 00:26:24.400
Is the boss himself?
Is the boss the employee?

00:26:24.400 --> 00:26:25.570
That's the question here.

00:26:25.570 --> 00:26:29.000
I mean, that's one of the big
questions of this chapter.

00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:31.030
When someone else causes you suffering...

00:26:31.030 --> 00:26:32.720
When your boss is yelling at you,

00:26:32.720 --> 00:26:35.370
who's yelling at you?

00:26:36.370 --> 00:26:38.520
Who caused it?

00:26:38.520 --> 00:26:41.640
Yeah, so you're hurting yourself.

00:26:41.640 --> 00:26:44.150
You're hurting yourself.

00:26:44.150 --> 00:26:46.560
Which we just said is impossible.

00:26:46.560 --> 00:26:47.735
Okay.

00:26:48.600 --> 00:26:52.203
Pain cannot hurt pain, right?

00:26:53.420 --> 00:26:54.630
Think about it.

00:26:54.630 --> 00:26:58.300
By the way, this whole
thing gets into blame.

00:26:58.300 --> 00:26:59.990
You know, can you blame other people

00:26:59.990 --> 00:27:02.320
for the trouble you have?

00:27:02.320 --> 00:27:05.300
Or what caused cancer?

00:27:05.300 --> 00:27:10.290
If the mantra's going to
work to stop the cancer,

00:27:10.290 --> 00:27:14.020
then it's going to have to stop
whatever caused the cancer.

00:27:14.020 --> 00:27:17.613
So then you got to look at
what really caused the cancer.

00:27:17.613 --> 00:27:21.460
Because if it's the mantra's
job to stop the cancer,

00:27:21.460 --> 00:27:25.008
the mantra's going to have to
stop what caused the cancer.

00:27:25.008 --> 00:27:28.259
Because if the mantra can't
stop what caused the cancer,

00:27:28.259 --> 00:27:30.780
then the more cancer's going to come.

00:27:30.780 --> 00:27:35.780
So does the mantra ever
work to stop cancer?

00:27:37.530 --> 00:27:41.310
Then it would have to stop the
cause of the cancer, right?

00:27:43.130 --> 00:27:45.220
And you have to think about that.

00:27:45.220 --> 00:27:48.040
How can the mantra touch
the cause of the cancer

00:27:48.040 --> 00:27:51.073
when the cause of the
cancer is already gone.

00:27:52.570 --> 00:27:56.153
How can you ever cure
cancer with a mantra?

00:27:58.678 --> 00:28:00.320
You would have to stop
the cause of the cancer

00:28:00.320 --> 00:28:02.790
which is already gone, anyway.

00:28:02.790 --> 00:28:04.290
You don't need the mantras to stop

00:28:04.290 --> 00:28:05.876
the cause of the cancer

00:28:05.876 --> 00:28:06.709
because the cause of the cancer

00:28:06.709 --> 00:28:09.230
is already gone by the
time the cancer's there.

00:28:09.230 --> 00:28:10.810
So how are you going to stop the cancer

00:28:10.810 --> 00:28:13.718
if you can't stop the cause of the cancer?

00:28:15.420 --> 00:28:17.180
How can you make contact with a thing

00:28:17.180 --> 00:28:19.243
which is already in the past?

00:28:20.220 --> 00:28:21.930
That's like writing your great grandma

00:28:21.930 --> 00:28:24.662
a letter or something.

00:28:24.662 --> 00:28:25.653
Okay?

00:28:26.500 --> 00:28:28.640
Therefore, the way a mantra works

00:28:28.640 --> 00:28:32.450
to stop your cancer is not what you think.

00:28:32.450 --> 00:28:34.570
You have to collect other seeds.

00:28:34.570 --> 00:28:37.880
And again, saving life is great.

00:28:37.880 --> 00:28:39.950
Saving some fish's life is good.

00:28:41.260 --> 00:28:43.140
And I think it gets you out of your house

00:28:43.140 --> 00:28:44.480
and it gets you actually saving

00:28:44.480 --> 00:28:46.550
a living being who's in front of you.

00:28:46.550 --> 00:28:50.640
And there's nothing as powerful as that.

00:28:50.640 --> 00:28:54.410
But I think there are also
lifestyle choices you can make:

00:28:54.410 --> 00:28:58.680
about using your car

00:28:58.680 --> 00:29:03.680
or using plastic, or things
like that, cutting down trees.

00:29:04.040 --> 00:29:06.240
That would save a lot more lives.

00:29:06.240 --> 00:29:09.260
Maybe you could do both.

00:29:09.260 --> 00:29:10.593
All right.

00:29:11.590 --> 00:29:13.160
All right, next verse.

00:29:13.160 --> 00:29:17.950
He puts together five, six, and seven.

00:29:17.950 --> 00:29:19.483
Here we go.

00:29:20.644 --> 00:29:21.852
,GAL TE GANG ZAG GZHAN LAS NI,

00:29:21.852 --> 00:29:23.510
,SDUG BSNGAL 'BYUNG NA GZHAN ZHIG GIS,

00:29:23.510 --> 00:29:25.585
,SDUG BSNGAL DE BYAS GANG SBYIN DE,

00:29:25.585 --> 00:29:28.940
,SDUG BSNGAL MA GTOGS JI LTAR RUNG,

00:29:28.940 --> 00:29:31.696
If the pain I have is caused

00:29:31.696 --> 00:29:33.804
GAL TE GANG ZAG GZHAN LAS NI

00:29:33.804 --> 00:29:36.379
if another person can cause me pain,

00:29:36.379 --> 00:29:40.880
SDUG BSNGAL 'BYUNG NA GZHAN ZHIG GIS

00:29:40.880 --> 00:29:45.290
then the suffering they
caused me should never stop.

00:29:45.290 --> 00:29:46.420
- Why?

00:29:46.420 --> 00:29:49.130
- Because if the pain, if the trouble

00:29:49.130 --> 00:29:52.870
in my life is really
caused by another person,

00:29:52.870 --> 00:29:57.050
then the word "another" means
a person who is not myself.

00:29:57.050 --> 00:29:58.510
- Right, right.

00:29:58.510 --> 00:30:01.240
- So a person who is not myself caused me

00:30:01.240 --> 00:30:02.820
some trouble in my life.

00:30:02.820 --> 00:30:06.311
- Right. - That means they
must have touched you.

00:30:07.920 --> 00:30:09.320
- Right.

00:30:09.320 --> 00:30:12.850
- If they never make
contact with you in any way,

00:30:12.850 --> 00:30:14.580
then they can't cause you trouble, right?

00:30:14.580 --> 00:30:15.420
- Right.

00:30:15.420 --> 00:30:17.830
- So they must have, their
life must've made contact

00:30:17.830 --> 00:30:19.460
with your life in some way, right?

00:30:19.460 --> 00:30:20.440
- Right.

00:30:20.440 --> 00:30:22.720
- So they must overlap
at some point, right?

00:30:22.720 --> 00:30:24.100
- No, they just touched me.

00:30:24.100 --> 00:30:25.430
They don't overlap.

00:30:25.430 --> 00:30:28.730
- Okay. So how do they touch
you without overlapping?

00:30:28.730 --> 00:30:33.478
- Well, just the edge of them
touches the edge of my trouble.

00:30:33.478 --> 00:30:35.170
- Come on, then there has to be contact.

00:30:35.170 --> 00:30:37.500
There has to be some overlap.

00:30:37.500 --> 00:30:39.220
- Okay. So there is overlap, Geshe-la.

00:30:39.220 --> 00:30:43.000
- Then the other person and your trouble

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:45.520
are partly the same thing.

00:30:45.520 --> 00:30:47.800
And any time the person's
there that give you trouble,

00:30:47.800 --> 00:30:50.242
I guess there are people like that.

00:30:51.094 --> 00:30:52.643
,GAL TE GANG ZAG GZHAN SDUG BSNGAL,

00:30:52.643 --> 00:30:54.093
,'BYUNG NA GANG GIS DE BYAS NAS,

00:30:54.093 --> 00:30:55.935
,GZHAN LA STER BA'I GANG ZAG GZHAN,

00:30:55.935 --> 00:30:59.160
,SDUG BSNGAL MA GTOGS GANG ZHIG YIN,

00:30:59.160 --> 00:31:02.835
- According to you someone
else is causing the trouble,

00:31:02.835 --> 00:31:03.849
problems in your life.

00:31:03.849 --> 00:31:05.370
- Yes, it's my partner.

00:31:05.370 --> 00:31:07.690
I don't have trouble.
They give me trouble.

00:31:07.690 --> 00:31:09.690
- Okay, so somebody else
gives you trouble, right?

00:31:09.690 --> 00:31:10.620
- Right.

00:31:10.620 --> 00:31:12.050
- So they have to make contact

00:31:12.050 --> 00:31:14.040
with you on some level, right?

00:31:14.040 --> 00:31:15.270
They have to make contact

00:31:15.270 --> 00:31:17.520
with you to give you trouble, right?

00:31:17.520 --> 00:31:18.353
- Yeah.

00:31:18.353 --> 00:31:23.352
- So in some way, at some
point they become you.

00:31:24.260 --> 00:31:27.160
The past touches the present.

00:31:27.160 --> 00:31:30.250
So the last part of the
past is the first part

00:31:30.250 --> 00:31:32.530
of the present because
the last part of the past

00:31:32.530 --> 00:31:35.160
has to start your trouble, right?

00:31:35.160 --> 00:31:36.677
By the way, if the other person

00:31:36.677 --> 00:31:41.550
and your trouble starting
were one millisecond apart,

00:31:41.550 --> 00:31:43.690
then they couldn't make contact.

00:31:43.690 --> 00:31:46.140
There's no point at
which they make contact.

00:31:46.140 --> 00:31:49.790
The cause is gone, the result is starting.

00:31:49.790 --> 00:31:51.896
- Well, that doesn't make sense

00:31:51.896 --> 00:31:55.210
because if the cause causes the result,

00:31:55.210 --> 00:32:00.210
then the cause has to share some
milliseconds with the result.

00:32:00.661 --> 00:32:03.160
Or else something which is not there

00:32:03.160 --> 00:32:05.160
is causing something which is there.

00:32:05.160 --> 00:32:07.068
And that's not possible.

00:32:07.068 --> 00:32:08.810
That's like a billiard ball

00:32:08.810 --> 00:32:10.810
that already fell in the pocket

00:32:10.810 --> 00:32:12.850
is making another ball move.

00:32:12.850 --> 00:32:14.460
See what I mean? It has to be there.

00:32:14.460 --> 00:32:17.650
They have to both be on the table.

00:32:17.650 --> 00:32:22.210
So the person who causes
you trouble in your life

00:32:22.210 --> 00:32:25.000
has to be in the same moment

00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:28.190
and in the same place as you to do that.

00:32:28.190 --> 00:32:31.300
- Yeah. - So that means
they're not a cause, right?

00:32:31.300 --> 00:32:32.805
- Why not?

00:32:32.805 --> 00:32:34.230
- Because they're past already.

00:32:34.230 --> 00:32:37.240
By the time the tree grows from a seed,

00:32:37.240 --> 00:32:38.830
the seed is gone.

00:32:38.830 --> 00:32:41.240
By the time your partner
gives you trouble,

00:32:41.240 --> 00:32:42.620
and you got the trouble,

00:32:42.620 --> 00:32:45.890
your partner has to be
invisible, not there.

00:32:45.890 --> 00:32:49.130
An invisible, non-existent partner,

00:32:49.130 --> 00:32:52.240
like a seed that disappeared
after the tree grew,

00:32:52.240 --> 00:32:54.570
is causing you trouble, right?

00:32:57.150 --> 00:32:58.045
Okay.

00:32:58.045 --> 00:32:59.370
,BDAG GIS BYAS PAR MA GRUB PAS,

00:32:59.370 --> 00:33:01.845
,SDUG BSNGAL GZHAN GYIS GA LA BYAS,

00:33:03.011 --> 00:33:05.677
,GZHAN GYIS SDUG BSNGAL GANG BYED PA,

00:33:05.677 --> 00:33:08.750
,DE NI DE YI BDAG BYAS 'GYUR,

00:33:08.750 --> 00:33:10.580
So the other guy is...

00:33:12.341 --> 00:33:16.227
This is now Choney Lama goes
off on a bit of a tangent.

00:33:16.227 --> 00:33:18.073
And I'll go with him.

00:33:22.130 --> 00:33:25.830
He says, "When I say your current pain

00:33:25.830 --> 00:33:27.870
"is caused by somebody else,

00:33:27.870 --> 00:33:32.210
"I just mean the actions taken by

00:33:32.210 --> 00:33:35.750
"a life form in the past, say an animal,

00:33:35.750 --> 00:33:39.520
"are causing the pain
of a human in this life.

00:33:39.520 --> 00:33:42.000
"So I'm not talking about the same person.

00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:44.980
That was an animal, this was a human."

00:33:44.980 --> 00:33:48.070
"I'm talking about different
life forms," he says.

00:33:48.070 --> 00:33:50.280
That's possible.

00:33:50.280 --> 00:33:51.840
They're not me.

00:33:51.840 --> 00:33:54.398
The animal is a different life form,

00:33:54.398 --> 00:33:55.500
somebody other than me.

00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:57.890
When I say somebody other
than me has caused me

00:33:57.890 --> 00:34:00.330
the trouble in this life I'm saying

00:34:00.330 --> 00:34:02.870
this human life's trouble was caused

00:34:02.870 --> 00:34:06.050
by someone who was an
animal, or something.

00:34:06.050 --> 00:34:09.650
That's the other guy's trying to say.

00:34:09.650 --> 00:34:13.770
Then you should have
suffering all the time.

00:34:13.770 --> 00:34:17.650
If someone can cause you suffering,

00:34:17.650 --> 00:34:21.620
if someone can give you trouble
without making contact with you,

00:34:21.620 --> 00:34:23.760
then you should have trouble all the time.

00:34:23.760 --> 00:34:24.760
- Why?

00:34:24.760 --> 00:34:27.080
- Because they're always
not making contact with you.

00:34:27.080 --> 00:34:29.210
Then your whole life
should be trouble all time.

00:34:29.210 --> 00:34:30.380
I'll say it again.

00:34:30.380 --> 00:34:34.070
If someone can give you trouble
without making contact with you,

00:34:34.070 --> 00:34:37.320
then even when they're not
around, you should have trouble.

00:34:37.320 --> 00:34:38.255
- Why?

00:34:38.255 --> 00:34:39.904
- Because they don't have to make contact

00:34:39.904 --> 00:34:43.187
with you to give you trouble.

00:34:45.270 --> 00:34:47.890
Then I chose a picture here.

00:34:50.780 --> 00:34:54.920
Do you ever give pain to your future self?

00:34:54.920 --> 00:34:57.645
There you go, there's the answer.

00:34:57.645 --> 00:34:58.478
Yeah, yeah.

00:34:58.478 --> 00:35:02.280
I don't know, yesterday
I made sweet rolls.

00:35:02.280 --> 00:35:06.760
Someone was teaching me to make
cinnamon rolls for our cafe.

00:35:06.760 --> 00:35:08.510
Then I don't know why we all felt,

00:35:08.510 --> 00:35:10.388
there were four of us there,

00:35:10.388 --> 00:35:12.480
and we all felt that
because we were making them

00:35:12.480 --> 00:35:16.127
for a noble purpose we could
eat them as much as we wanted.

00:35:16.127 --> 00:35:19.484
And we all ate like
three or four of those.

00:35:19.484 --> 00:35:21.710
And then afterwards I was like,

00:35:21.710 --> 00:35:24.370
what the heck did I just do?

00:35:27.083 --> 00:35:30.670
Yeah, I am causing pain
for my future self.

00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:33.220
But how is that if I never touched them?

00:35:33.220 --> 00:35:36.010
If I'm gone, if the person who ate

00:35:36.010 --> 00:35:38.690
the three or four cinnamon rolls is gone

00:35:38.690 --> 00:35:41.460
by the time the other person gets fat,

00:35:41.460 --> 00:35:43.190
then can you really say that someone

00:35:43.190 --> 00:35:46.020
who's not there is giving someone trouble

00:35:46.020 --> 00:35:48.255
to someone who is there?

00:35:48.255 --> 00:35:49.648
It's not possible.

00:35:49.648 --> 00:35:51.250
It's actually not possible.

00:35:51.250 --> 00:35:53.930
- Well, Geshe-la, what's really going on?

00:35:53.930 --> 00:35:55.810
Some kind of karmic seed is creating

00:35:55.810 --> 00:35:59.720
the eating the cinnamon roll.

00:35:59.720 --> 00:36:03.000
And then another karmic seed
is creating the fat person.

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:05.360
But the cinnamon roll
doesn't cause the fat person.

00:36:05.360 --> 00:36:08.850
In theory, you should be
able to eat cinnamon rolls

00:36:08.850 --> 00:36:11.110
without getting fat.

00:36:11.110 --> 00:36:14.260
We're still looking for the sweet spot.

00:36:15.700 --> 00:36:16.533
All right.

00:36:18.570 --> 00:36:20.300
Let's go onto the next verse.

00:36:20.300 --> 00:36:21.260
And I know it's hard.

00:36:21.260 --> 00:36:24.682
It's hard to have so much
Nagarjuna in one day.

00:36:24.682 --> 00:36:26.223
Hang in there.

00:36:28.403 --> 00:36:30.194
,RE ZHIG SDUG BSNGAL BDAG BYAS MIN,

00:36:30.194 --> 00:36:32.402
,DE NYID KYIS NI DE MA BYAS,

00:36:32.402 --> 00:36:35.736
,GAL TE GZHAN BDAG MA BYAS NA,

00:36:35.736 --> 00:36:39.933
,SDUG BSNGAL GZHAN BYAS GA LA 'GYUR,

00:36:39.933 --> 00:36:42.639
RE ZHIG SDUG BSNGAL BDAG
GIS BYAS PA MIN PAR THAL

00:36:42.639 --> 00:36:45.250
SDUG BSNGAL DE NYID KYIS
NI DE MA BYAS PA'I PHYIR

00:36:45.250 --> 00:36:48.470
You can't say that pain causes pain

00:36:48.470 --> 00:36:52.290
because the pain that
causes the present pain

00:36:52.290 --> 00:36:54.028
would have to be past pain

00:36:54.028 --> 00:36:56.965
and that past pain would have to be gone.

00:36:56.965 --> 00:36:59.748
RANG GIS RANG NA BYED PA 'GAL BA'I PHYIR,

00:36:59.748 --> 00:37:03.098
GAL TE SDUG BSNGAL GZHAN
BDAG GIS MA BYAS NA

00:37:03.098 --> 00:37:05.673
SDUG BSNGAL DE GZHAN
GYIS BYAS PAR SMRA BA'ANG

00:37:05.673 --> 00:37:07.098
GA LA 'GYUR TE

00:37:07.098 --> 00:37:09.460
If I didn't cause my own pain,

00:37:09.460 --> 00:37:11.110
and something else caused my own pain,

00:37:11.110 --> 00:37:12.900
but also that thing was gone by

00:37:12.900 --> 00:37:14.580
the time I had my own pain,

00:37:14.580 --> 00:37:16.780
and something that was
gone was causing something

00:37:16.780 --> 00:37:18.288
that's not gone.

00:37:19.370 --> 00:37:20.203
Okay.

00:37:21.430 --> 00:37:25.623
So the picture I have
here is, I don't know why.

00:37:27.300 --> 00:37:30.561
No one can cause me pain.

00:37:30.561 --> 00:37:32.710
I cannot.

00:37:32.710 --> 00:37:36.950
Michael cannot cause
Michael pain by overeating.

00:37:36.950 --> 00:37:39.620
Michael at three o'clock
cannot cause trouble

00:37:39.620 --> 00:37:42.930
for Michael at four o'clock by
over eating at three o'clock.

00:37:42.930 --> 00:37:43.763
- Why?

00:37:43.763 --> 00:37:45.650
Because Michael who
overeats at three o'clock

00:37:45.650 --> 00:37:48.360
is gone by the time Michael
at four o'clock is suffering.

00:37:48.360 --> 00:37:51.663
They never touched.
They never made contact.

00:37:53.430 --> 00:37:55.580
So I cannot cause myself pain.

00:37:55.580 --> 00:37:58.412
Obviously, if someone else
cooks me cinnamon rolls

00:37:58.412 --> 00:37:59.370
and I eat too many of them,

00:37:59.370 --> 00:38:01.524
since they never touched me

00:38:01.524 --> 00:38:02.868
they didn't cause me the pain, either.

00:38:02.868 --> 00:38:03.701
Therefore, I didn't have the pain?

00:38:03.701 --> 00:38:05.930
- No, I had the pain.

00:38:05.930 --> 00:38:09.250
It was coming from somewhere else.

00:38:09.250 --> 00:38:11.686
All right, here we go.

00:38:11.686 --> 00:38:14.188
GAL TE, next verse.

00:38:14.188 --> 00:38:15.404
,GAL TE RE RES BYAS GYUR NA,

00:38:15.404 --> 00:38:16.787
,SDUG BSNGAL GNYIS KAS BYAS PAR 'GYUR,

00:38:16.787 --> 00:38:18.912
,BDAG GIS MA BYAS GZHAN MA BYAS,

00:38:18.912 --> 00:38:21.170
,SDUG BSNGAL RGYU MED GA LA 'GYUR,

00:38:21.170 --> 00:38:23.810
Then he skips over quickly
the other two possibilities.

00:38:23.810 --> 00:38:24.643
- Why?

00:38:26.090 --> 00:38:26.923
Say again?

00:38:28.098 --> 00:38:30.530
- [Woman] Both and neither.
- Yeah, both and neither.

00:38:30.530 --> 00:38:35.403
Both Geshe-la and somebody else
causes Geshe-la to get overweight.

00:38:37.543 --> 00:38:40.250
Or nobody causes Geshe-la
to get overweight.

00:38:40.250 --> 00:38:43.420
Neither Geshe-la nor
anyone else causes Geshe-la

00:38:43.420 --> 00:38:44.764
to get overweight.

00:38:44.764 --> 00:38:46.950
And he just dismisses those two.

00:38:46.950 --> 00:38:47.783
Okay.

00:38:50.280 --> 00:38:51.471
Picture?

00:38:58.580 --> 00:39:02.172
It's a picture of two hands
solving a puzzle, I think.

00:39:04.950 --> 00:39:09.530
Yeah, anyway, it's not both me
and someone else causing my pain.

00:39:09.530 --> 00:39:12.980
And it's not nobody causing my pain.

00:39:12.980 --> 00:39:15.210
Nobody causing my pain is easy.

00:39:15.210 --> 00:39:18.420
- But Geshe-la, how can
you say that it's not me

00:39:18.420 --> 00:39:20.968
and somebody else causing my pain?

00:39:20.968 --> 00:39:23.060
Because they are gone by
the time you have the pain.

00:39:23.060 --> 00:39:27.160
And something that's not
there cannot cause pain.

00:39:27.160 --> 00:39:29.846
All right, here we keep going, next verse.

00:39:32.172 --> 00:39:33.755
,SDUG BSNGAL 'BA' ZHIG RNAM PA BZHI,

00:39:33.755 --> 00:39:35.947
,YOD MA YIN PAR MA ZAD KYI,

00:39:35.947 --> 00:39:37.963
,PHYI ROL DNGOS PO DAG LA YANG,

00:39:37.963 --> 00:39:39.813
,RNAM PA BZHI PO YOD MA YIN,

00:39:41.520 --> 00:39:44.420
He says, "Look, we just
finished a discussion

00:39:44.420 --> 00:39:47.160
of suffering from four points of view."

00:39:47.160 --> 00:39:49.290
Does suffering cause suffering?

00:39:49.290 --> 00:39:51.500
Does something else cause suffering?

00:39:51.500 --> 00:39:54.670
Does both itself and something
else cause suffering?

00:39:54.670 --> 00:39:57.843
Or does suffering happen "ahetuka",

00:39:58.880 --> 00:40:00.837
"without any cause at all".

00:40:00.837 --> 00:40:01.903
And he said no.

00:40:01.903 --> 00:40:03.943
He said no to all four.

00:40:04.930 --> 00:40:07.450
Then he said, "Take that principle

00:40:07.450 --> 00:40:10.133
and apply it to everything
else in your life."

00:40:10.133 --> 00:40:12.330
PHYI ROL DNGOS PO RNAMS LA YANG

00:40:12.330 --> 00:40:15.510
Apply it to all the things
around you in your world.

00:40:15.510 --> 00:40:17.850
All the things around you in your world

00:40:17.850 --> 00:40:20.460
are also not caused by themselves,

00:40:20.460 --> 00:40:22.390
are not caused by something else,

00:40:22.390 --> 00:40:25.750
are not caused by both, and
are not caused by nothing.

00:40:25.750 --> 00:40:28.230
But they are caused, so
how does that happen?

00:40:28.230 --> 00:40:30.880
From seeds in your mind.

00:40:30.880 --> 00:40:34.830
You create, your mind creates the cause.

00:40:34.830 --> 00:40:36.940
Your mind creates the result.

00:40:36.940 --> 00:40:40.070
Your mind creates the connection
between the cause and the result,

00:40:40.070 --> 00:40:42.490
but the cause doesn't cause the result.

00:40:42.490 --> 00:40:44.633
That's a fallacy. That's wrong.

00:40:45.660 --> 00:40:47.530
That means that everything everyone

00:40:47.530 --> 00:40:49.010
has ever done on this planet

00:40:49.010 --> 00:40:51.450
who didn't understand
emptiness was mistaken.

00:40:51.450 --> 00:40:56.230
Every action taken in the
last few million years

00:40:56.230 --> 00:40:59.530
by any person in the world was mistaken

00:40:59.530 --> 00:41:01.590
and didn't do what it was supposed to do.

00:41:01.590 --> 00:41:04.601
It had no relationship
to what they wanted.

00:41:05.680 --> 00:41:08.460
Every single action in human history

00:41:08.460 --> 00:41:10.503
was worthless and useless.

00:41:14.594 --> 00:41:15.427
All right.

00:41:17.140 --> 00:41:20.890
And that is the joyful
end of this first class.

00:41:20.890 --> 00:41:24.240
Every action taken by any living being,

00:41:24.240 --> 00:41:28.120
animal or human, in the
history of this world

00:41:28.120 --> 00:41:30.670
if they didn't understand these things,

00:41:30.670 --> 00:41:32.743
was useless and wrong.

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:37.635
Okay, see you guys in the next class.

